# Copy style: no em dashes

Never use an em dash (`—`) in user-facing copy. That includes page body text, headings, metadata descriptions, structured data strings, alt text, and UI labels.

Use a comma, colon, period, or a short rewrite instead.

```text
❌ multiple CMS platforms — including WordPress and WP Engine — so teams can move quickly
✅ multiple CMS platforms, including WordPress and WP Engine, so teams can move quickly

❌ for a reason — editorial workflows, plugins, and familiarity
✅ for a reason: editorial workflows, plugins, and familiarity

❌ as a contractor or team hire — themes, plugins, and ACF
✅ as a contractor or team hire: themes, plugins, and ACF
```

Do not substitute an en dash (`–`) or `--` for the same pause. Rewrite the sentence so it reads cleanly without a dash.
